// Stand-in for the now-UNCONDITIONAL text.cla manifest entry (Plan 5b Task
// 9) in this fake runtime-module directory (Task 4's inclusion-machinery
// test, internal/lowlevel/rtinc_test.go). Deliberately empty, same reason
// as this directory's str.cla stand-in: this directory exercises expand's
// declare-before-use splicing machinery, not text.cla's real content -- the
// real module lives at runtime/clarus/text.cla. main.cla now always adds
// "text.cla" to neededMods regardless of usage flags, so --rtdir
// testdata/rtinc/rt needs SOME file by that name (an empty/decl-less file
// pushes main.cla's own "-1 head" empty-file sentinel, already handled) or
// TestRtInc's IncludesRuntimeModule/NoInclusionWithoutUsage subtests fail
// with "runtime module text.cla not found" before ever reaching the
// assertions they actually care about.
